Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Two work tapes suffice (stated), the per-run alphabet
 reduction, and the efficient universal machine

- Turing.FinTM.alphabet_reduction_run: alphabet reduction run by run, with the converse
  (proved from the block simulation's run correspondence).
- Turing.exists_code2TM: every two-work-tape binary machine has a coded equivalent.
- Robustness/TwoTapes: Turing.FinTM.two_work_tapes_run (Hennie-Stearns, stated with sorry)
  and two_work_tapes_binary (proved from it).
- UniversalTlogT: Turing.universal_TlogT, AB09 Theorem 1.9 at T log T, per run and with the
  converse, proved from two_work_tapes_run, exists_code2TM and universalK.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
